module Collections

### Suflae SF-realm Collections circular list — roam-boundary wrapper over a bare RF::Collections.CircularList[T].
### Entity + default constructor hand-written; every other method auto-forwarded (SuflaeForwarders).
###
### **When to use** — want a stack, queue, or deque? Suflae has no separate types for these;
### `CircularList[T]` is all three. Stack: `add_last` / `remove_last!`. Queue: `add_last` /
### `remove_first!`. Deque: insert and remove at either end. Its sharpest edge: a bounded
### "keep the latest N" history in fixed space via `add_last_keeping(value, keeping: n)` (or `add_last`
### then `keep_last(n)`) — no reallocation, which `List[T]` cannot do in O(1).
entity CircularList[T]
  secret inner: RF::Collections.CircularList[T]

routine CircularList[T]() -> CircularList[T]
  return CircularList[T](inner: RF::Collections.CircularList[T]())
